WEBVTT

STYLE
::cue(c.color9CD5FF) { color: #9CD5FF; }

1
00:00:01.000 --> 00:00:07.000 line:5% align:center
<b><c.color9CD5FF>One Pace Addon</c></b>

2
00:01:50.050 --> 00:01:54.010
<b>Ohara vs. The World Government</b>

3
00:01:59.540 --> 00:02:01.580
What's the matter, Robin?

4
00:02:01.580 --> 00:02:02.980
You have to tell me.

5
00:02:02.980 --> 00:02:05.650
Did my mom come by here?

6
00:02:05.650 --> 00:02:06.820
Now hold on a minute.

7
00:02:06.820 --> 00:02:08.520
Where did that come from?

8
00:02:08.520 --> 00:02:11.450
Why would you think your
mother was back in Ohara?

9
00:02:11.720 --> 00:02:13.060
I've severed all bonds.

10
00:02:13.060 --> 00:02:17.030
No matter what, I can't let her
become the daughter of a criminal.

11
00:02:17.810 --> 00:02:21.490
I wish she was here,
too, but she's not.

12
00:02:21.490 --> 00:02:23.230
Oh yeah! We're in trouble!

13
00:02:23.230 --> 00:02:26.030
I heard there are Navy battleships
coming to the island right now!

14
00:02:26.030 --> 00:02:28.570
They're trying to get rid of
all the scholars on Ohara!

15
00:02:28.570 --> 00:02:31.980
The people in town must
be stirring up bad rumors.

16
00:02:31.980 --> 00:02:33.110
Huh?

17
00:02:33.110 --> 00:02:37.380
The truth is, that's no battleship and
they won't be "getting rid of anyone".

18
00:02:37.380 --> 00:02:39.850
The Government is
paying us a visit, though.

19
00:02:39.850 --> 00:02:43.890
And that means the library will be
under an investigation, a harsh one.

20
00:02:43.890 --> 00:02:44.960
So listen up.

21
00:02:44.960 --> 00:02:47.410
No matter what those
government agents say or do,

22
00:02:47.410 --> 00:02:48.910
you absolutely cannot let them know

23
00:02:48.910 --> 00:02:51.580
that you're an archaeologist
like the rest of us.

24
00:02:51.580 --> 00:02:53.960
Since you're so young,
as long as you keep quiet,

25
00:02:53.960 --> 00:02:55.620
no one will think you're a scholar.

26
00:02:55.620 --> 00:02:57.790
You understand?

27
00:02:58.660 --> 00:03:01.430
Move it!

28
00:03:01.430 --> 00:03:02.360
Stop what you're doing!

29
00:03:02.360 --> 00:03:04.930
Put your hands in
the air and go outside!

30
00:03:04.930 --> 00:03:06.950
Don't you think you're
being a bit violent?

31
00:03:06.950 --> 00:03:10.200
The researchers here at the Tree
of Knowledge are being charged

32
00:03:10.200 --> 00:03:12.900
with the heinous crime
of deciphering Poneglyphs.

33
00:03:12.900 --> 00:03:14.070
We'll be investigating the library,

34
00:03:14.070 --> 00:03:17.020
so everyone get out of our
way and leave the building!

35
00:03:17.020 --> 00:03:19.210
You'd better treat
this place with care.

36
00:03:19.210 --> 00:03:23.480
The value of this collection is well
beyond your imagination, I assure you.

37
00:03:23.480 --> 00:03:25.750
I don't have to listen
to a word you say!

38
00:03:25.750 --> 00:03:26.450
Take 'em outside!

39
00:03:26.450 --> 00:03:27.760
Yes sir!

40
00:03:27.760 --> 00:03:29.530
Attention, citizens of Ohara.

41
00:03:29.530 --> 00:03:31.720
I regret to inform you that
the scholars of this island

42
00:03:31.720 --> 00:03:35.250
may be devils in disguise,
plotting to destroy the world!

43
00:03:35.670 --> 00:03:36.510
What?

44
00:03:36.510 --> 00:03:37.650
But why?

45
00:03:37.650 --> 00:03:39.580
Our scholars are the pride of
every person in Ohara-

46
00:03:39.580 --> 00:03:41.850
they would never dream of
doing something like that!

47
00:03:41.850 --> 00:03:43.620
From this point forward,
we will be conducting

48
00:03:43.620 --> 00:03:45.950
a large-scale search
of the entire island!

49
00:03:45.950 --> 00:03:48.090
During that time,
all those who are not related

50
00:03:48.090 --> 00:03:50.720
to the research center must
take a form of identification

51
00:03:50.720 --> 00:03:53.920
and head to the evacuation
ship on the west seashore.

52
00:03:53.920 --> 00:03:54.990
Evacuation?

53
00:03:54.990 --> 00:03:55.960
That's ridiculous!

54
00:03:55.960 --> 00:04:00.060
Even if the scholars did do something wrong,
that still has nothing to do with us!

55
00:04:00.060 --> 00:04:02.130
You can't kick us off our own island!

56
00:04:02.130 --> 00:04:05.890
Our only obligation was to
pass on this message to you.

57
00:04:05.890 --> 00:04:09.560
Disregard our warning if you like,
but we won't be held responsible

58
00:04:09.560 --> 00:04:13.370
should any unfortunate
"accidents" occur.

59
00:04:18.360 --> 00:04:19.130
You heard him!

60
00:04:19.730 --> 00:04:21.380
Everyone, head to the west shore!

61
00:04:21.380 --> 00:04:23.180
I don't want to have
any part of this mess!

62
00:04:28.090 --> 00:04:28.960
I've been shot!

63
00:04:28.960 --> 00:04:30.680
This is it for me!

64
00:04:30.680 --> 00:04:32.080
I'm a goner, damn it!

65
00:04:32.080 --> 00:04:34.320
A goner! Contact the higher ups.

66
00:04:34.320 --> 00:04:37.060
Tell them I want my
son to take over for me!

67
00:04:37.060 --> 00:04:38.840
Calm down Chief...just take a look.

68
00:04:38.840 --> 00:04:41.160
The bullet went through
your sleeve, that's all.

69
00:04:41.160 --> 00:04:42.930
Oh. I see.

70
00:04:45.700 --> 00:04:47.240
I'll aim to kill next time.

71
00:04:47.240 --> 00:04:49.910
Well, if it isn't Nico Olvia!

72
00:04:49.910 --> 00:04:52.810
I find it hard to believe that
a devious criminal like you

73
00:04:52.810 --> 00:04:56.910
would end up on this island completely
by coincidence after your daring escape!

74
00:04:56.910 --> 00:04:59.920
In other words, despite the fact
that you've denied your connection

75
00:04:59.920 --> 00:05:02.890
to the scholars of Ohara, you've
shown up at their doorstep

76
00:05:02.890 --> 00:05:06.000
just in time to warn them
of our little investigation.

77
00:05:06.000 --> 00:05:10.900
Now in my humble opinion, that very clearly
labels them as your partners in crime.

78
00:05:10.900 --> 00:05:12.790
You've no idea why I'm here.

79
00:05:12.790 --> 00:05:14.760
That doesn't prove one single thing.

80
00:05:14.760 --> 00:05:16.020
Hmph.

81
00:05:16.020 --> 00:05:18.820
I'm sure you've cooked up plenty
of excuses to cover for them.

82
00:05:18.820 --> 00:05:21.090
You're a clever woman, after all.

83
00:05:21.090 --> 00:05:24.190
But that doesn't really matter, because
we don't have to prove your connection

84
00:05:24.190 --> 00:05:26.810
to the Ohara scholars anymore.

85
00:05:26.810 --> 00:05:29.920
Now that we're here, we can search
every little nook and cranny.

86
00:05:29.920 --> 00:05:33.930
I doubt it'll take long before we find
evidence of their Poneglyph research.

87
00:05:33.930 --> 00:05:37.860
The government's quite confident in
this and you know they're never wrong.

88
00:05:37.860 --> 00:05:40.300
This has been in the
works for a long time.

89
00:05:40.560 --> 00:05:44.980
Capturing you after 6 years of hide and
seek was nothing more than the final push.

90
00:05:44.980 --> 00:05:47.170
There are plenty of Poneglyph
researchers around the world

91
00:05:47.170 --> 00:05:48.340
and each time we captured one,

92
00:05:50.020 --> 00:05:53.770
we tried to find any connection
they might have to Ohara.

93
00:05:53.770 --> 00:05:56.070
Can you guess why that is?

94
00:05:56.570 --> 00:05:59.140
Don't tell me, you're
making an example of us?

95
00:05:59.140 --> 00:06:00.610
Exactly!

96
00:06:00.610 --> 00:06:03.670
If we crush this
"holy ground of archaeology",

97
00:06:03.670 --> 00:06:06.070
the entire academic
world will take notice.

98
00:06:06.070 --> 00:06:08.010
It's the perfect opportunity
to show the world

99
00:06:08.010 --> 00:06:11.810
exactly what happens to those
who research the Blank Century.

100
00:06:11.810 --> 00:06:16.360
Then, the battleships from headquarters
waiting on standby are here to...

101
00:06:16.360 --> 00:06:18.100
Well look at that!

102
00:06:18.100 --> 00:06:20.400
You are a clever woman, aren't you?

103
00:06:20.400 --> 00:06:25.780
Yes, as you might guess, they're to ensure
that not even a single criminal escapes.

104
00:06:25.780 --> 00:06:29.410
However, as a matter of form,
we still need to verify their guilt.

105
00:06:29.410 --> 00:06:31.820
We aren't pirates, after all.

106
00:06:31.820 --> 00:06:35.050
So, I came all this way to conduct
a compulsory investigation

107
00:06:35.050 --> 00:06:38.490
of the island and chase off
anyone who's not involved.

108
00:06:38.490 --> 00:06:40.820
It's curtains for you and your friends.

109
00:06:40.820 --> 00:06:42.580
There's no escape.

110
00:06:43.640 --> 00:06:45.510
Take her down.

111
00:06:56.620 --> 00:06:57.520
Hey, what're you doing?

112
00:06:57.520 --> 00:06:59.590
All the books here are world treasures!

113
00:06:59.590 --> 00:07:01.460
Take him outside and shut him up!

114
00:07:01.460 --> 00:07:02.400
Move it!

115
00:07:02.400 --> 00:07:03.500
You bastards!

116
00:07:03.500 --> 00:07:05.620
They must have a secret room
somewhere around here!

117
00:07:05.620 --> 00:07:07.660
Don't stop until you find it!

118
00:07:07.410 --> 00:07:11.330
<b>Northwest Coastline, Ohara
(Saul's Present Location)</b>

119
00:07:11.980 --> 00:07:14.630
This is worse than I thought!

120
00:07:14.630 --> 00:07:18.630
The battleships are here already
and there's a whole mess of 'em!

121
00:07:20.680 --> 00:07:22.240
That should be everyone!

122
00:07:22.240 --> 00:07:24.240
Good! Now don't let them go anywhere!

123
00:07:25.840 --> 00:07:27.840
Look! They're rounding
up all the scholars!

124
00:07:27.840 --> 00:07:29.210
What did they do wrong?

125
00:07:29.210 --> 00:07:32.020
They say they were cooking up
a plan to destroy the world!

126
00:07:32.020 --> 00:07:33.160
That can't be true!

127
00:07:33.160 --> 00:07:35.590
Where is the evacuation ship?

128
00:07:35.590 --> 00:07:37.460
It's on the west seashore! Hurry!

129
00:07:37.460 --> 00:07:39.000
Everyone run!

130
00:07:39.000 --> 00:07:40.490
Who knows what might happen!

131
00:07:40.490 --> 00:07:43.990
Robin. They said there's
an evacuation ship waiting.

132
00:07:43.990 --> 00:07:46.460
We don't know what the government
is going to do anymore,

133
00:07:46.460 --> 00:07:48.290
you should get out while you can.

134
00:07:48.290 --> 00:07:49.400
No way!

135
00:07:49.400 --> 00:07:52.070
There's nothing but mean
people on that stupid boat!

136
00:07:52.320 --> 00:07:54.000
I'm staying here with my friends!

137
00:07:54.000 --> 00:07:54.870
Robin.

138
00:07:54.870 --> 00:07:58.370
I'm the same as you...
That's enough, just go!

139
00:07:59.320 --> 00:08:02.750
Looks like you have the
situation under control!

140
00:08:02.750 --> 00:08:04.190
Thank you very much, chief!

141
00:08:04.190 --> 00:08:06.090
I was quite surprised.

142
00:08:06.090 --> 00:08:10.690
Nobody warned me there were such
ferocious beasts wandering the island!

143
00:08:13.280 --> 00:08:16.190
But it makes for a fine trophy, huh?

144
00:08:17.590 --> 00:08:18.700
Olvia.

145
00:08:18.700 --> 00:08:20.740
All right, listen carefully.

146
00:08:22.570 --> 00:08:24.600
This woman is an escaped prisoner.

147
00:08:24.600 --> 00:08:26.670
We executed her
comrades after we found out

148
00:08:26.670 --> 00:08:29.340
that they'd been
deciphering ancient texts.

149
00:08:29.340 --> 00:08:32.280
But we still have a couple
of matters left to clear up.

150
00:08:32.280 --> 00:08:34.280
So let me be frank here.

151
00:08:34.280 --> 00:08:36.510
If she's your partner,
just come out with it already,

152
00:08:36.510 --> 00:08:39.220
so I can get this
over with and go home.

153
00:08:40.450 --> 00:08:43.320
How awful of them to
hurt someone like that.

154
00:08:43.320 --> 00:08:47.320
Robin, for the last time, go! Hurry!

155
00:08:47.320 --> 00:08:49.390
Robin?

156
00:08:53.700 --> 00:08:55.500
Robin!

157
00:08:58.060 --> 00:09:01.130
My little girl.

158
00:09:04.370 --> 00:09:06.470
You've grown so much!

159
00:09:07.330 --> 00:09:13.230
Olvia.

160
00:09:13.230 --> 00:09:14.500
Wh-what are they doing?

161
00:09:14.500 --> 00:09:17.200
If they're not careful, they're
gonna burn the whole tree down!

162
00:09:17.200 --> 00:09:19.610
I never thought they would
take such drastic measures!

163
00:09:19.610 --> 00:09:22.480
Wow, they aren't
holding back, are they?

164
00:09:24.990 --> 00:09:26.960
Hello? Is this the Chief?

165
00:09:26.960 --> 00:09:28.360
Yeah. It's me.

166
00:09:28.360 --> 00:09:30.090
We found a hidden room in the basement!

167
00:09:30.090 --> 00:09:32.930
They have a huge tablet there,
probably a Poneglyph,

168
00:09:32.930 --> 00:09:36.610
and a massive collection of research
documents discussing the ancient texts!

169
00:09:36.610 --> 00:09:38.400
Nice work!

170
00:09:38.400 --> 00:09:40.000
Click.

171
00:09:42.040 --> 00:09:48.480
Well, scholars of Ohara, I'm afraid your
death sentence has already been decided!

172
00:09:48.480 --> 00:09:52.590
It's a pity. I hate to
lose so many fine scholars,

173
00:09:52.590 --> 00:09:55.590
but you're really
forcing my hand, here!

174
00:10:00.490 --> 00:10:02.230
Wow, what a letdown.

175
00:10:02.230 --> 00:10:04.570
I came all this way just to say that?

176
00:10:04.570 --> 00:10:07.700
Guess we'd better report
to the Five Elder Stars.

177
00:10:07.700 --> 00:10:09.540
Roger.

178
00:10:09.540 --> 00:10:12.160
Professor, they aren't
really going to kill you?

179
00:10:12.160 --> 00:10:15.560
They wouldn't do that to someone just
for learning about history, would they?

180
00:10:15.560 --> 00:10:16.310
Stupid brat!

181
00:10:16.310 --> 00:10:17.580
What do you know?

182
00:10:17.580 --> 00:10:19.760
They may say they're "learning
about history", but the truth is

183
00:10:19.760 --> 00:10:23.740
they're learning how to revive an ancient
weapon so they can commit mass murder!

184
00:10:23.740 --> 00:10:24.620
You're wrong!

185
00:10:24.620 --> 00:10:26.720
They would never do anything like that!

186
00:10:26.720 --> 00:10:28.260
Don't bother, Robin.

187
00:10:28.260 --> 00:10:31.290
It's pointless to discuss the matter
with an errand boy like him.

188
00:10:31.290 --> 00:10:32.120
What's that?

189
00:10:32.120 --> 00:10:36.020
Is it really the ancient weapon itself
that the World Government is afraid of?

190
00:10:36.020 --> 00:10:36.530
Professor!

191
00:10:36.530 --> 00:10:37.230
Be careful!

192
00:10:37.230 --> 00:10:38.780
They're on the line now, Chief.

193
00:10:38.780 --> 00:10:39.430
Good.

194
00:10:39.430 --> 00:10:40.130
Hold on!

195
00:10:41.130 --> 00:10:41.930
Huh?

196
00:10:41.930 --> 00:10:46.510
Before you put all of us to death allow
me to speak to the Five Elder Stars.

197
00:10:46.510 --> 00:10:48.250
Although we still have much to learn,

198
00:10:48.250 --> 00:10:51.350
we have proudly continued
our research for many years.

199
00:10:51.350 --> 00:10:54.120
So at the very least, I would
like to share our hypothesis

200
00:10:54.120 --> 00:10:56.820
on the Blank Century
with the world's leaders.

201
00:10:57.540 --> 00:10:59.460
Stubborn old fart. Hey!

202
00:10:59.460 --> 00:11:00.320
Yes sir?

203
00:11:00.320 --> 00:11:02.560
I'm begging you,
please get out of here.

204
00:11:02.560 --> 00:11:05.660
If you hear what I have to say,
you'll become a criminal.

205
00:11:06.630 --> 00:11:08.500
Professor.

206
00:11:08.500 --> 00:11:11.510
Hey, it looks like they found
the people from the library guilty!

207
00:11:11.510 --> 00:11:12.840
You gotta be kidding me!

208
00:11:12.840 --> 00:11:13.870
Bad news!

209
00:11:13.870 --> 00:11:16.770
There's a bunch of Navy battleships
closing in on the island from the east!

210
00:11:16.770 --> 00:11:18.410
This is about to get real ugly!

211
00:11:18.410 --> 00:11:20.410
We'd better evacuate now!

212
00:11:20.970 --> 00:11:22.130
What is that?

213
00:11:22.130 --> 00:11:24.000
It's a giant!

214
00:11:26.800 --> 00:11:29.270
Where are you, Robin?

215
00:11:29.640 --> 00:11:32.810
You gotta get off this
island before it's too late!

216
00:11:39.300 --> 00:11:41.610
Have they made the order
for the Buster Call yet?

217
00:11:41.610 --> 00:11:43.580
We're still on standby.

218
00:11:43.580 --> 00:11:45.780
Hurry!

219
00:11:45.780 --> 00:11:48.680
Run to the evacuation ship!

220
00:11:51.660 --> 00:11:53.960
So this is a Poneglyph, huh?

221
00:11:53.960 --> 00:11:54.630
Yeah.

222
00:11:54.630 --> 00:11:55.860
I heard even if we shoot it

223
00:11:55.860 --> 00:11:58.530
with a cannon it won't leave
a single scratch on the thing.

224
00:11:58.530 --> 00:12:01.900
I can't believe these creepy things
are hidden all over the world.

225
00:12:01.900 --> 00:12:03.550
I don't like it.

226
00:12:03.980 --> 00:12:04.980
Is that so?

227
00:12:04.980 --> 00:12:06.210
Yes.

228
00:12:06.210 --> 00:12:07.710
The evidence is clear.

229
00:12:07.710 --> 00:12:10.380
This calls for nothing
short of the death penalty.

230
00:12:10.380 --> 00:12:12.090
We're waiting for your order.

231
00:12:12.090 --> 00:12:13.830
It's unfortunate.

232
00:12:13.830 --> 00:12:18.400
But seeing as they've broken the law so
blatantly, there's really no other option.

233
00:12:18.400 --> 00:12:20.840
We must enforce our own rules.

234
00:12:20.840 --> 00:12:23.440
We don't need your mock
sympathy, Elder Stars.

235
00:12:23.440 --> 00:12:25.270
Save your breath.

236
00:12:25.270 --> 00:12:28.210
You're talking to the leaders of
the world, you damned criminal!

237
00:12:28.210 --> 00:12:29.450
Show some respect!

238
00:12:29.450 --> 00:12:31.350
That must be Professor Clover.

239
00:12:31.350 --> 00:12:34.390
Ohara's foremost authority
on archaeology.

240
00:12:34.390 --> 00:12:36.360
I'm familiar with your work.

241
00:12:36.360 --> 00:12:39.600
You've contributed much to
the world's cultural heritage.

242
00:12:39.600 --> 00:12:42.390
It's sad to see a man of
your intellect go astray.

243
00:12:42.390 --> 00:12:45.400
The history of this planet
belongs to all of mankind.

244
00:12:46.250 --> 00:12:48.050
No matter what that history may be,

245
00:12:48.050 --> 00:12:51.250
you don't have the right to
forbid us from learning it.

246
00:12:51.250 --> 00:12:52.880
No one does.

247
00:12:52.880 --> 00:12:54.210
Professor.

248
00:12:54.210 --> 00:12:56.480
If one can read the Poneglyphs,
then it's also possible

249
00:12:56.480 --> 00:13:00.780
that they can revive the ancient weapons
and place the world in serious peril.

250
00:13:00.780 --> 00:13:03.200
Even if you have
the best of intentions,

251
00:13:03.200 --> 00:13:06.870
someone else could come along
and use your research for evil.

252
00:13:07.590 --> 00:13:10.660
Be it good or bad, mankind
has the responsibility

253
00:13:10.660 --> 00:13:13.660
to accept whatever
their history may hold.

254
00:13:13.660 --> 00:13:16.130
As long as we don't succumb
to fear and ignorance,

255
00:13:16.130 --> 00:13:18.770
we will be prepared for
anything that may come.

256
00:13:18.770 --> 00:13:19.940
That's idealistic.

257
00:13:19.940 --> 00:13:20.870
Is it?

258
00:13:20.870 --> 00:13:24.270
Or are you just making convenient
excuses to suit your needs?

259
00:13:25.110 --> 00:13:28.680
In truth, there are two
mysteries left unsolved.

260
00:13:28.680 --> 00:13:32.360
Of course we want to read the Poneglyphs,
but the reason why they were made

261
00:13:32.360 --> 00:13:35.270
in the first place is
interesting as well.

262
00:13:35.270 --> 00:13:37.180
Why was their message so important,

263
00:13:37.180 --> 00:13:42.120
that they had to inscribe it on unbreakable
stone to pass on to future generations?

264
00:13:42.120 --> 00:13:45.120
Why were they hidden and
scattered across the world?

265
00:13:45.120 --> 00:13:47.930
Why were they not stored in a library?

266
00:13:47.930 --> 00:13:51.170
The only logical conclusion is
that they feared their message

267
00:13:51.170 --> 00:13:55.280
would be too easily destroyed
if they had written it on paper.

268
00:13:55.280 --> 00:13:57.610
In other words, they had an enemy.

269
00:13:57.610 --> 00:14:01.510
Someone who was afraid of the
information they wanted to pass on.

270
00:14:03.140 --> 00:14:06.310
What are you trying to
imply, Professor Clover?

271
00:14:06.310 --> 00:14:08.290
Since the Ancients have disappeared,

272
00:14:08.290 --> 00:14:11.230
we must assume that they
were defeated by this enemy,

273
00:14:11.230 --> 00:14:15.100
and that whoever they were,
they survived through history.

274
00:14:16.970 --> 00:14:21.110
It may be no coincidence, that
roughly 800 years in the past,

275
00:14:21.110 --> 00:14:24.460
when the Blank Century came
to an end, the organization

276
00:14:24.460 --> 00:14:28.170
we now call "The World
Government" was founded.

277
00:14:30.850 --> 00:14:34.240
Therefore, if this unknown enemy
was indeed the World Government,

278
00:14:34.240 --> 00:14:35.440
it might be in their best interest

279
00:14:35.440 --> 00:14:38.780
to "erase" this inconvenient
piece of information and let

280
00:14:38.780 --> 00:14:42.810
the ancients disappear into a
fabricated "Blank Century".

281
00:14:42.810 --> 00:14:45.330
By analyzing ancient manuscripts
and piecing together what we

282
00:14:45.330 --> 00:14:48.900
could from the few Poneglyphs
we were able to find, we

283
00:14:48.900 --> 00:14:52.400
discovered the existence of
a previously unknown country.

284
00:14:52.400 --> 00:14:55.260
Although the details we
found were a bit scarce,

285
00:14:55.260 --> 00:14:58.260
we believe it was a
grand and powerful kingdom.

286
00:14:58.260 --> 00:15:01.500
And yet, despite their
strength, not a trace remains.

287
00:15:01.500 --> 00:15:04.690
Or rather, those traces
were deliberately erased.

288
00:15:04.690 --> 00:15:06.700
But they were prepared
for this possibility,

289
00:15:06.700 --> 00:15:09.740
even as they faced
the threat of extinction.

290
00:15:09.740 --> 00:15:11.710
And so they etched their
history in stone,

291
00:15:11.710 --> 00:15:14.540
before their kingdom was
crushed under the might

292
00:15:14.540 --> 00:15:17.580
of the allied nations now known
as the World Government.

293
00:15:17.580 --> 00:15:21.610
Thus, the reason why the Poneglyphs
were made becomes quite clear.

294
00:15:21.610 --> 00:15:23.320
I see.

295
00:15:23.320 --> 00:15:25.390
That's a bold hypothesis.

296
00:15:25.390 --> 00:15:29.090
It's true that the ancient weapons
would be a threat to the world.

297
00:15:29.090 --> 00:15:33.040
But more so than weapons, what I believe
the World Government is afraid of

298
00:15:33.040 --> 00:15:35.470
is the history surrounding
this lost kingdom.

299
00:15:35.470 --> 00:15:38.340
Its existence and its ideologies
are so dangerous to you,

300
00:15:38.340 --> 00:15:41.140
that you would kill
to keep them secret.

301
00:15:41.580 --> 00:15:43.110
Although we still don't
know what makes you

302
00:15:43.110 --> 00:15:46.050
fear this kingdom, we do
at least know its name.

303
00:15:46.050 --> 00:15:50.820
Since we've gone so far already, perhaps
you'd like me to share it with you now?

304
00:15:51.940 --> 00:15:53.710
Kill him!

305
00:16:03.790 --> 00:16:06.630
Professor!

306
00:16:08.790 --> 00:16:11.760
You left us no choice.

307
00:16:13.600 --> 00:16:14.300
You bastards!

308
00:16:14.300 --> 00:16:15.500
How dare you!

309
00:16:16.710 --> 00:16:17.870
Professor!

310
00:16:17.870 --> 00:16:20.610
Ohara knows too much.

311
00:16:22.050 --> 00:16:24.850
You may give the order to attack.

312
00:16:25.530 --> 00:16:27.000
Don't move an inch!

313
00:16:27.670 --> 00:16:29.640
You mustn't let anyone escape.

314
00:16:37.320 --> 00:16:42.490
Now then, with the golden transponder
snail entrusted to me by Admiral Sengoku.

315
00:16:42.490 --> 00:16:43.930
Professor!

316
00:16:44.580 --> 00:16:46.460
Robin, you fool.

317
00:16:46.460 --> 00:16:49.000
I told you to run. Hurry!

318
00:16:49.000 --> 00:16:52.190
I invoke the Buster Call!

319
00:16:52.190 --> 00:16:53.610
And, that's a wrap.

320
00:16:53.610 --> 00:16:55.440
He pressed something!

321
00:16:55.440 --> 00:16:57.620
What is that?

322
00:16:57.620 --> 00:17:00.430
Get out of here! Go!

323
00:17:00.430 --> 00:17:02.530
No! I don't want to be alone!

324
00:17:02.530 --> 00:17:04.710
You have to stop being so selfish.

325
00:17:04.710 --> 00:17:06.910
This isn't the time!

326
00:17:09.350 --> 00:17:11.190
Robin.

327
00:17:09.970 --> 00:17:14.390
<b>Silver Transponder Snail
Receiver for the Golden Transponder Snail</b>

328
00:17:12.680 --> 00:17:14.180
It's the Buster Call!

329
00:17:14.180 --> 00:17:16.480
All battleships, to your positions!

330
00:17:16.480 --> 00:17:18.620
Prepare to open fire!

331
00:17:20.640 --> 00:17:23.510
What? Hey, look!

332
00:17:23.510 --> 00:17:26.660
The Tree of Knowledge is on fire!

333
00:17:26.660 --> 00:17:28.430
Damn it! What're you doing?

334
00:17:28.430 --> 00:17:29.220
Are you insane?

335
00:17:29.220 --> 00:17:32.130
Isn't it enough to take our lives?

336
00:17:32.910 --> 00:17:34.150
Hey, it's not my fault.

337
00:17:34.150 --> 00:17:37.380
Must've caught fire when they
bombed your secret basement.

338
00:17:38.870 --> 00:17:40.400
Stop this! Right now!

339
00:17:40.400 --> 00:17:42.400
You can't replace
the documents in there!

340
00:17:42.400 --> 00:17:43.340
Don't you realize that?

341
00:17:43.340 --> 00:17:44.540
You! Don't move!

342
00:17:44.540 --> 00:17:48.140
Whoa, we don't need guns anymore.

343
00:17:48.440 --> 00:17:51.580
Time for the government
agents to pull out.

344
00:17:52.410 --> 00:17:54.280
Protect the books.

345
00:17:56.080 --> 00:17:58.490
Let's put out the fire! Hurry!

346
00:18:08.090 --> 00:18:09.860
Pass the water over here!

347
00:18:11.700 --> 00:18:14.870
Carry as many books outside as you can!

348
00:18:28.110 --> 00:18:30.550
Bring that woman with you.

349
00:18:31.330 --> 00:18:33.800
Get up.

350
00:18:33.800 --> 00:18:35.930
There's still some info we
have to wring out of her.

351
00:18:35.930 --> 00:18:37.440
She can't die yet.

352
00:18:37.440 --> 00:18:40.270
Just make sure she
doesn't escape again.

353
00:18:43.080 --> 00:18:44.540
Mommy!

354
00:18:49.620 --> 00:18:53.160
Please Robin, run while you still can!

355
00:18:53.160 --> 00:18:57.430
You can't die here! Not like this!

356
00:18:57.430 --> 00:18:59.360
Funny nose!

357
00:19:02.300 --> 00:19:04.650
Go! We're done for!

358
00:19:04.650 --> 00:19:06.550
There's no point in staying!

359
00:19:09.860 --> 00:19:11.260
Robin!

360
00:19:11.260 --> 00:19:12.790
Robin, don't.

361
00:19:20.400 --> 00:19:23.770
You're my mother, aren't you?

362
00:19:28.400 --> 00:19:29.860
Make up your mind, Olvia!

363
00:19:29.860 --> 00:19:31.870
Are you going to
board this ship or not?

364
00:19:31.870 --> 00:19:33.900
Mommy!

365
00:19:33.900 --> 00:19:34.970
I'm holding her back!

366
00:19:34.970 --> 00:19:37.380
Just hurry and get on!

367
00:19:37.380 --> 00:19:41.980
Mommy! Mommy! No! Mommy!

368
00:19:41.980 --> 00:19:43.540
I'm sorry, Robin.

369
00:19:43.540 --> 00:19:45.620
I can never call myself
your mother again.

370
00:19:45.620 --> 00:19:48.490
After all these years,
after all I've done,

371
00:19:49.590 --> 00:19:52.030
I don't have the right anymore.

372
00:19:57.100 --> 00:19:58.100
Monster!

373
00:20:01.980 --> 00:20:03.090
Monster!

374
00:20:03.090 --> 00:20:05.890
She's so scary her mom ran away!

375
00:20:05.890 --> 00:20:07.590
Hey, that's my daughter's dress!

376
00:20:07.590 --> 00:20:08.520
You take it off!

377
00:20:08.520 --> 00:20:09.760
I'm sorry, Aunt Roji!

378
00:20:09.760 --> 00:20:11.630
I just wanted to try it on!

379
00:20:11.630 --> 00:20:14.430
You sure eat a lot for a freeloader.

380
00:20:22.550 --> 00:20:24.780
Please, answer me.

381
00:20:25.680 --> 00:20:28.080
Are you my mom?

382
00:20:33.830 --> 00:20:35.530
Hm? Hold on.

383
00:20:35.530 --> 00:20:38.300
That girl your daughter or what?

384
00:20:39.650 --> 00:20:41.700
No.

385
00:20:41.700 --> 00:20:42.900
Olvia.

386
00:20:44.000 --> 00:20:46.000
I'm sorry, little girl.

387
00:20:46.000 --> 00:20:50.340
You must be confusing
me with someone else.

388
00:20:51.110 --> 00:20:55.880
Even if it comes to this, I don't want
you to be the daughter of a criminal.

389
00:20:55.880 --> 00:20:57.650
Olvia.

390
00:20:57.650 --> 00:21:01.950
What a weird little brat.
Right, let's go!

391
00:21:16.350 --> 00:21:18.720
It's me! It's Robin!

392
00:21:18.720 --> 00:21:23.490
I've grown since the last time
so maybe you don't recognize me?

393
00:21:23.490 --> 00:21:26.400
I've been waiting
for you all these years!

394
00:21:26.400 --> 00:21:28.230
Are you sure?

395
00:21:29.030 --> 00:21:30.370
You're really...

396
00:21:32.070 --> 00:21:34.140
...not my mom?

397
00:21:34.810 --> 00:21:39.430
Just once, someday,
I wanted to hold your hand,

398
00:21:39.430 --> 00:21:43.040
and walk together like a family.

399
00:21:43.470 --> 00:21:48.510
I studied hard to become an archaeologist,
so I could go to sea with you!

400
00:21:48.510 --> 00:21:51.270
I can read the Poneglyphs, too!

401
00:21:52.330 --> 00:21:53.560
What did she say?

402
00:21:53.560 --> 00:21:55.530
Robin! No!

403
00:21:56.220 --> 00:21:58.470
So please, look at me!

404
00:21:58.470 --> 00:22:02.690
Let me stay with you! Mom!

405
00:22:02.690 --> 00:22:04.120
Robin!

406
00:22:05.500 --> 00:22:07.330
I've waited so long.

407
00:22:08.290 --> 00:22:10.390
We're finally together.

408
00:22:10.390 --> 00:22:12.690
Don't leave me alone again!

409
00:22:18.300 --> 00:22:20.270
Oh no! Now what's going on?

410
00:22:21.080 --> 00:22:24.120
Now commencing the Buster Call.

411
00:22:24.120 --> 00:22:25.680
All ships, fire at once.

412
00:22:25.680 --> 00:22:28.690
Everything on the island
of Ohara is your target.

413
00:22:28.690 --> 00:22:30.750
Let nothing remain.

414
00:22:30.750 --> 00:22:34.640
The research conducted here was far
more extensive than we anticipated.

415
00:22:34.640 --> 00:22:37.250
Make sure that knowledge
is not passed on.

416
00:22:37.250 --> 00:22:39.520
Do not allow it to leave the island.

417
00:22:39.520 --> 00:22:42.210
Annihilate the devils of Ohara!

418
00:22:42.210 --> 00:22:43.310
Burn it to the ground!

419
00:22:43.310 --> 00:22:45.950
In the name of justice!

420
00:22:49.350 --> 00:22:50.050
Damn it!

421
00:22:50.050 --> 00:22:51.950
What the hell?

422
00:22:51.950 --> 00:22:53.760
Can't you wait 'til
we leave the island?

423
00:22:53.760 --> 00:22:57.060
You're gonna kill us! Stop it!

424
00:22:57.560 --> 00:22:59.960
The Tree of Knowledge
took a direct hit!

425
00:22:59.960 --> 00:23:02.610
They're using their
highest power against us.

426
00:23:02.610 --> 00:23:06.300
They stage their investigation,
but they were planning this from the start.

427
00:23:06.300 --> 00:23:07.180
Bastards.

428
00:23:07.180 --> 00:23:08.150
Hey, chief.

429
00:23:08.150 --> 00:23:10.420
That girl said she can
read the Poneglyphs.

430
00:23:10.420 --> 00:23:12.420
Yeah, she did, didn't she?

431
00:23:12.420 --> 00:23:14.050
I don't know if it's
true or not, though.

432
00:23:14.050 --> 00:23:16.500
Probably safer to wipe
her out, just in case.

433
00:23:16.500 --> 00:23:18.140
Don't let her leave the island.

434
00:23:18.140 --> 00:23:20.190
Remember her face, all right?

435
00:23:20.190 --> 00:23:21.340
We're retreating!

436
00:23:21.340 --> 00:23:23.240
Then I'll grab Olvia.

437
00:23:24.500 --> 00:23:25.360
Screw it!

438
00:23:25.360 --> 00:23:27.450
The situation has changed. Just run!

439
00:23:27.450 --> 00:23:30.250
I'm not gonna get blown up trying
to follow some stupid order!

440
00:23:30.250 --> 00:23:33.330
Our number one priority
is keeping me alive!

441
00:23:33.330 --> 00:23:34.300
Retreat!

442
00:23:34.300 --> 00:23:36.530
Everyone, back to the ship!

443
00:23:44.560 --> 00:23:46.660
Put out the fire on that
side before it spreads!

444
00:23:46.660 --> 00:23:49.530
Protect the library at all costs!

445
00:24:09.800 --> 00:24:12.300
I've been waiting a
long time to do this.

446
00:24:14.230 --> 00:24:16.000
I'm glad.

447
00:24:20.150 --> 00:24:22.180
Robin!

448
00:24:24.130 --> 00:24:25.900
Mommy!

449
00:24:26.420 --> 00:24:28.520
Robin, forgive me.

450
00:24:30.920 --> 00:24:32.090
Please.

451
00:24:32.090 --> 00:24:36.420
This is my fault for not
watching over you with more care.

452
00:24:36.420 --> 00:24:40.060
Is it really true that you
can read the Poneglyphs?

453
00:24:40.480 --> 00:24:42.050
I had to learn.

454
00:24:42.050 --> 00:24:44.420
Since, I wanted to be a scholar.

455
00:24:44.420 --> 00:24:46.720
I never knew my little
girl was an archaelogist!

456
00:24:46.720 --> 00:24:48.190
That's amazing!

457
00:24:48.190 --> 00:24:51.520
You must've studied hard
while I was gone, huh?

458
00:24:51.520 --> 00:24:54.330
These aren't things that just
anyone can do!

459
00:24:54.330 --> 00:24:57.430
I'm so proud!

460
00:25:02.620 --> 00:25:03.720
Fortunately, the only ones who know

461
00:25:03.720 --> 00:25:06.870
about this are the officials
who were here earlier.

462
00:25:06.870 --> 00:25:09.460
We can't afford to waste any more time!

463
00:25:09.460 --> 00:25:11.760
Olvia! Take Robin and run!

464
00:25:11.760 --> 00:25:14.430
If you can sneak her
onto the evacuation ship,

465
00:25:14.430 --> 00:25:17.170
she might still be able
to leave the island!

466
00:25:20.450 --> 00:25:21.320
Robin!

467
00:25:21.320 --> 00:25:23.690
I've been looking all over for you!

468
00:25:23.690 --> 00:25:24.820
It's Saul!

469
00:25:24.820 --> 00:25:26.760
So you met with your mother after all.

470
00:25:26.760 --> 00:25:27.760
Saul!

471
00:25:27.760 --> 00:25:29.970
Why in the world are you here?

472
00:25:29.970 --> 00:25:31.640
Guess it must be fate!

473
00:25:31.640 --> 00:25:35.770
I just happened to wash up here and your
little girl was the one who found me.

474
00:25:35.770 --> 00:25:38.300
Anyhow, we ain't got
time to chat right now.

475
00:25:38.300 --> 00:25:40.700
You gotta get off this island!

476
00:25:40.700 --> 00:25:44.370
I'll be fine, but I need you take
care of Robin for me, please.

477
00:25:44.370 --> 00:25:46.470
Huh? But why? What about you?

478
00:25:46.470 --> 00:25:49.480
Aren't you going to come with me?

479
00:25:49.480 --> 00:25:50.710
Olvia, are you?

480
00:25:50.710 --> 00:25:52.250
I can't leave yet.

481
00:25:52.250 --> 00:25:53.580
There's something left to do.

482
00:25:53.580 --> 00:25:55.780
No, Mom! You can't leave me now!

483
00:25:55.780 --> 00:25:57.950
I'll stay here with you!

484
00:25:57.950 --> 00:26:00.020
I don't want to lose you again!

485
00:26:00.020 --> 00:26:02.590
Robin, if you're a scholar of Ohara,

486
00:26:02.590 --> 00:26:05.430
you should know that history
is mankind's greatest treasure.

487
00:26:05.430 --> 00:26:09.530
Now that it's been passed on, it will
illuminate the path to your future.

488
00:26:09.530 --> 00:26:12.260
However, you must pass it on as well.

489
00:26:12.260 --> 00:26:15.430
Or its light will disappear
with the next generation.

490
00:26:15.780 --> 00:26:16.860
Save those books!

491
00:26:16.860 --> 00:26:18.530
Someone take these!

492
00:26:18.530 --> 00:26:21.330
We weren't trying to
uncover some dark secret.

493
00:26:21.330 --> 00:26:24.580
We simply wanted to hear the voices
of the past and protect them.

494
00:26:24.580 --> 00:26:26.640
Unfortunately, our research ends here.

495
00:26:27.340 --> 00:26:30.980
But time marches on,
even if Ohara is destroyed.

496
00:26:32.150 --> 00:26:34.160
And as surely as we
believe in the past,

497
00:26:34.160 --> 00:26:37.260
we believe in the future
that you will inherit!

498
00:26:38.530 --> 00:26:40.300
What does that mean?

499
00:26:41.800 --> 00:26:45.670
Someday, you'll know.

500
00:26:46.740 --> 00:26:50.780
Hurry. Take her and go, Saul.

501
00:26:51.780 --> 00:26:53.320
Are you sure?

502
00:26:53.320 --> 00:26:55.120
Yeah.

503
00:26:55.120 --> 00:26:55.920
Stop it!

504
00:26:55.920 --> 00:27:01.530
I wanna stay with you! Mommy! No!

505
00:27:01.530 --> 00:27:04.730
I was happy to hear
you call me that again.

506
00:27:04.730 --> 00:27:09.600
Thank you. From now on,
for my sake as well.

507
00:27:09.600 --> 00:27:12.340
You must live, Robin!

508
00:27:30.500 --> 00:27:31.660
Vice Admiral Kuzan!

509
00:27:31.660 --> 00:27:33.230
What now?

510
00:27:33.230 --> 00:27:35.740
It looks like... no,
wait, it's gotta be!

511
00:27:35.740 --> 00:27:37.690
So are you gonna tell me, or not?

512
00:27:37.690 --> 00:27:39.500
Spit it out already, man!

513
00:27:39.500 --> 00:27:40.600
It's the deserter.

514
00:27:40.600 --> 00:27:41.930
Vice Admiral Saul!

515
00:27:41.930 --> 00:27:44.540
Please, Saul, you have to take me back!

516
00:27:44.540 --> 00:27:45.570
I can't!

517
00:27:45.570 --> 00:27:46.500
There's no way!

518
00:27:46.500 --> 00:27:48.330
Don't cry, Robin!

519
00:27:48.330 --> 00:27:51.150
Be proud! Your momma's
a wonderful woman!

520
00:27:51.150 --> 00:27:53.090
Ohara's a wonderful place!

521
00:27:53.090 --> 00:27:55.090
You gotta remember that!

522
00:27:55.090 --> 00:27:57.450
It's up to you to pass it on, okay?

523
00:27:57.450 --> 00:28:01.390
Ohara was so brave they
fought against the whole world!

524
00:28:04.760 --> 00:28:05.990
Are you crazy?

525
00:28:05.990 --> 00:28:07.840
Capturing them is enough!

526
00:28:07.840 --> 00:28:09.940
They ain't even pirates,
they're scholars!

527
00:28:09.940 --> 00:28:12.980
Are you so weak you can't reel
'em in without blowing 'em up?

528
00:28:12.980 --> 00:28:16.900
We shoot down these researcher
ships one after another,

529
00:28:16.900 --> 00:28:20.990
but I still can't find any sense
in killin' these poor folks.

530
00:28:20.990 --> 00:28:22.330
Vice Admiral Saul!

531
00:28:22.330 --> 00:28:24.660
We found a survivor!

532
00:28:24.660 --> 00:28:27.260
You're nothing but murderers!

533
00:28:27.860 --> 00:28:28.960
You're scholars.

534
00:28:28.960 --> 00:28:30.700
Why do you need ancient weapons?

535
00:28:30.700 --> 00:28:32.000
You don't know a thing!

536
00:28:32.000 --> 00:28:34.650
You don't even why you're killing us!

537
00:28:34.650 --> 00:28:36.050
That's a Vice Admiral
you're speaking to!

538
00:28:36.050 --> 00:28:37.670
The weapons are just an excuse!

539
00:28:37.670 --> 00:28:40.480
Why don't you try thinking about
what you're doing for once?

540
00:28:41.150 --> 00:28:45.230
You're just afraid of a past
that you know nothing about!

541
00:28:46.180 --> 00:28:47.950
This is a top-secret mission.

542
00:28:47.950 --> 00:28:49.580
The Buster Call?

543
00:28:49.580 --> 00:28:54.050
It's an all-out attack in which Five
Vice-Admirals command ten battleships.

544
00:28:54.050 --> 00:28:55.590
I want you to take part.

545
00:28:55.590 --> 00:28:57.060
They're just scholars, right?

546
00:28:57.060 --> 00:28:59.100
Why do we have to go so far?

547
00:28:59.100 --> 00:29:02.700
Even the ones we've captured before
don't seem like they care about weapons...

548
00:29:02.700 --> 00:29:04.850
they just wanna learn
more about history!

549
00:29:04.850 --> 00:29:09.110
If their research is so dangerous,
why don't we help them so nothing goes wrong?

550
00:29:09.110 --> 00:29:12.460
Least you can do is give me some
proof that these folks are bad!

551
00:29:12.460 --> 00:29:15.540
'Cause to me it seems like
we're the criminals here!

552
00:29:15.540 --> 00:29:17.110
Are you questioning the government?

553
00:29:17.110 --> 00:29:19.650
Just follow your orders!

554
00:29:23.010 --> 00:29:25.990
I got some questions for you.

555
00:29:25.990 --> 00:29:27.520
You think we can talk?

556
00:29:27.520 --> 00:29:28.690
This is an emergency!

557
00:29:28.690 --> 00:29:31.860
Vice Admiral Saul has taken
the prisoner and deserted!

558
00:29:31.860 --> 00:29:33.430
This won't do.

559
00:29:33.430 --> 00:29:35.880
He knows too much
about our next operation.

560
00:29:35.880 --> 00:29:36.630
After them.

561
00:29:36.630 --> 00:29:38.890
Stop Saul and Olvia at any cost.

562
00:29:38.890 --> 00:29:41.460
Open fire if necessary.

563
00:29:41.460 --> 00:29:45.040
Troops'll be showing up any minute
now, but I'll take care of 'em.

564
00:29:45.040 --> 00:29:48.020
You know, you won't be able to
return to the Navy after this.

565
00:29:48.020 --> 00:29:52.820
Fine by me. Now that I got this doubt in
my heart, ain't no point in staying anyway.

566
00:29:52.820 --> 00:29:57.210
I know the law's the law, but the way
they're acting this time is downright cruel.

567
00:29:57.210 --> 00:29:59.750
So I'm following my
own sense of justice.

568
00:29:59.750 --> 00:30:02.250
Now, you get to that island
and warn your friends.

569
00:30:02.250 --> 00:30:03.830
I'm not going to thank you.

570
00:30:03.830 --> 00:30:06.250
Well, good luck to you, either way.

571
00:30:06.250 --> 00:30:08.150
Fire!

572
00:30:13.650 --> 00:30:16.450
They're not targeting the
island, they're targeting me!

573
00:30:20.870 --> 00:30:22.830
Saul!

574
00:30:22.830 --> 00:30:24.000
Ah! It hit him!

575
00:30:24.000 --> 00:30:24.860
I'm sorry!

576
00:30:24.860 --> 00:30:26.430
Don't apologize!

577
00:30:26.430 --> 00:30:28.570
He's a criminal's accomplice now!

578
00:30:28.570 --> 00:30:29.970
My apologies, Robin.

579
00:30:30.740 --> 00:30:33.480
That musta scared you.

580
00:30:33.810 --> 00:30:36.050
Wait here a sec.

581
00:30:36.050 --> 00:30:37.680
Are you the one firing at us?

582
00:30:37.680 --> 00:30:41.630
What if you'd hurt that poor
little girl, you damn fools?

583
00:30:41.630 --> 00:30:43.240
Vice Admiral, please stop!

584
00:30:43.240 --> 00:30:44.040
What're you doing?

585
00:30:44.040 --> 00:30:45.570
I don't know about justice anymore.

586
00:30:45.570 --> 00:30:48.570
But I do know I can protect my friend!

587
00:30:48.570 --> 00:30:50.310
Stop it, Saul!

588
00:30:50.310 --> 00:30:51.480
You're scaring me!

589
00:30:51.480 --> 00:30:58.370
Hope you're ready 'cause if you make an enemy
outta me there's gonna be hell to pay!
